01:27:33.600 --> 01:27:36.340
Based on this and their sheer quantity,

01:27:36.340 --> 01:27:38.970
it seems clear to us what they're after.

01:27:38.970 --> 01:27:40.190
They want Earth.

01:27:40.190 --> 01:27:42.190
- You sure they don't want us, son?

01:27:42.190 --> 01:27:43.750
I thought their modus operandi

01:27:43.750 --> 01:27:45.900
was to use stars as incubators.

01:27:45.900 --> 01:27:47.380
- As far as they're concerned,

01:27:47.380 --> 01:27:49.830
stars are simply a means to an end.

01:27:49.830 --> 01:27:51.650
But they have been carefully eliminating

01:27:51.650 --> 01:27:54.360
all traces of humanity wherever they find us.

01:27:54.360 --> 01:27:57.450
For instance, if you were to look at us as a bacteria

01:27:57.450 --> 01:27:59.670
in a larger system such as our galaxy,

01:28:00.320 --> 01:28:04.780
They would be the antibodies that exist to hunt down and destroy us.

01:28:04.780 --> 01:28:07.120
That's absurd!

01:28:07.120 --> 01:28:09.090
You think so?

01:28:09.090 --> 01:28:14.950
If you consider things on a cosmic scale, humanity serves no real practical purpose whatsoever.

01:28:14.950 --> 01:28:18.950
We drift through the ether, not to produce, only consume.

01:28:18.950 --> 01:28:20.960
Less than trash.

01:28:20.960 --> 01:28:30.000
Have you gotten to try the Andromeda cake scene?

01:28:30.440 --> 01:28:31.240
Not yet.

01:28:31.240 --> 01:28:34.160
Really? Then we should go get some after this.

01:28:34.160 --> 01:28:35.610
Huh?

01:28:35.610 --> 01:28:37.430
Noriko, wanna come?

01:28:37.430 --> 01:28:40.320
Sorry, I still have trash duty today.

01:28:40.320 --> 01:28:41.830
Uh...

01:28:41.830 --> 01:28:48.400
She just seems so distant lately.

01:28:48.400 --> 01:28:52.760
I don't think that's it. It's just that ever since Kazumi dumped her, she's moved on.

01:28:52.760 --> 01:28:54.520
Huh? Who's she with now then?

01:28:54.520 --> 01:28:57.430
Wait, you haven't seen her sneaking off to be with Coach?

01:28:57.430 --> 01:28:59.890
I bet the two of them are hooking up right now.

01:29:02.430 --> 01:29:05.380
So it's true that you asked Coach to split you up with Noriko?

01:29:05.380 --> 01:29:06.970
Hmm...

01:29:06.970 --> 01:29:09.830
Well, maybe I'll go ask for a date!

01:29:09.830 --> 01:29:11.070
Eh?

01:29:11.070 --> 01:29:15.330
I met with Noriko!

01:29:36.560 --> 01:29:41.510
- You're late, where have you been?

01:29:41.510 --> 01:29:44.800
Let's review what we covered yesterday.

01:29:44.800 --> 01:29:46.990
From the turn-up to break-off.

01:29:46.990 --> 01:29:48.790
You've got three minutes.

01:29:51.190 --> 01:29:58.900
- One, two.

01:29:58.900 --> 01:29:59.730
- Too slow.

01:30:00.060 --> 01:30:03.600
The enemy could reach the moon from Mars in three minutes!

01:30:03.600 --> 01:30:06.090
Takea, I want you to remember this.

01:30:06.090 --> 01:30:08.700
You're the only one who will protect you.

01:30:08.700 --> 01:30:13.020
Never be the fool who sacrifices themselves for someone else.

01:30:13.020 --> 01:30:17.450
If you absolutely must save someone, fight for your own life in the process.

01:30:17.450 --> 01:30:18.500
Sir!

01:30:18.500 --> 01:30:21.260
Good. Now show me Form C. 50 reps!

01:30:21.260 --> 01:30:21.800
Yes!

01:30:30.220 --> 01:30:35.100
What a surprise running into you here. I thought you went to go get and draw me the cakes with the others

01:30:37.160 --> 01:30:48.790
No, not this time. I'm sure they probably just forgot to mention it. Looks like you've been training pretty hard lately, haven't you?

01:30:49.490 --> 01:30:52.390
Wanna put those new skills to the test?

01:30:52.570 --> 01:31:00.000
You're suggesting we fight. I hope you know that it wouldn't be very fair. Are you implying I'd lose that easel?

01:31:01.560 --> 01:31:02.560
Why would you say that?

01:31:02.560 --> 01:31:04.060
Huh, you think I'm an idiot?

01:31:04.060 --> 01:31:08.570
Everyone knows you've been getting special treatment from Koj, so you can pilot that new mech!

01:31:08.570 --> 01:31:09.910
Yeah, but...

01:31:09.910 --> 01:31:14.330
Stand there and tell me your fight with Kazumi wasn't just a stunt.

01:31:14.330 --> 01:31:22.590
No more excuses. I want to see what you're capable of.

01:31:22.590 --> 01:31:26.630
If you insist.

01:31:34.380 --> 01:31:39.300
We'll use dummy ammo, just like in Trainink. They won't explode, but they'll pack quite a punch.

01:31:39.840 --> 01:31:40.940
So don't hold back.

01:31:41.580 --> 01:31:42.180
Got it.

01:31:44.130 --> 01:31:46.790
Kolch gives her everything on a silver platter.

01:31:48.200 --> 01:31:50.910
I didn't even have a chance. It's bullshit!

01:31:51.980 --> 01:31:54.670
I'm a gunbuster pilot. That's all there is to it.

01:31:55.260 --> 01:32:00.000
Regardless what Ms. Amano or Jung or any of the others think, this is who I am now.

01:32:01.400 --> 01:32:04.230
- Smith, I won't forget my promise.

01:32:36.590 --> 01:32:56.090
What the f*** are you doing out there with her?

01:32:56.640 --> 01:32:57.760
Nothing, really.

01:32:58.340 --> 01:33:00.000
I just wanted to see which of us

01:33:00.000 --> 01:33:04.320
the better pilot. But, looks like I didn't need to bother.

01:33:09.600 --> 01:33:14.340
Are you really that jealous of her? You're pathetic.

01:33:14.340 --> 01:33:20.320
Don't act like you're better than me. We both know in the end he chose Noriko over you.

01:33:20.320 --> 01:33:27.620
But he still needs to get her to pilot, and then she'll die. Assuming she can even go back into space.

01:33:30.410 --> 01:33:32.350
I know.

01:33:32.350 --> 01:33:34.130
I'll die.

01:33:34.130 --> 01:33:36.710
Guess I'll see you soon.

01:33:36.710 --> 01:33:38.360
Smith!

01:33:38.360 --> 01:33:51.040
So, what did you want to ask?

01:33:51.040 --> 01:33:54.870
When will you stop forcing Noriko to go along with this plan of yours?

01:34:00.320 --> 01:34:02.700
When this is over, all of it.

01:34:03.700 --> 01:34:06.480
The gunbuster was originally designed with me in mind.

01:34:06.800 --> 01:34:08.780
Don't you think you're asking too much of her?

01:34:10.600 --> 01:34:12.870
You can rein in the arrogance, thank you.

01:34:13.330 --> 01:34:15.570
The plan has always been for you to have a co-pilot.

01:34:16.090 --> 01:34:18.690
You worry about you. I'll worry about Takaya.

01:34:19.020 --> 01:34:21.620
If anyone here is being arrogant, it's you.

01:34:22.290 --> 01:34:25.730
However badly you want it, you can't force someone to be something they're not.

01:34:25.730 --> 01:34:30.000
I understand that you want revenge for what they took from you, but whatever...

01:34:30.060 --> 01:34:41.750
you need I should be enough. Please leave Noriko out of this. Thank you, sir. That's all I'm going

01:34:41.750 --> 01:34:51.580
to say. I don't believe that. All I know is that if you send her out, she's not coming back. How do

01:34:51.580 --> 01:34:57.060
you expect someone to save us when they can't even protect themselves? Coach, you can't spill milk

01:34:57.060 --> 01:34:59.180
and then expect to put it back in the glass.

01:35:00.280 --> 01:35:07.920
Amano what to your brilliant point when you spill milk you can pour another that's all I'll say

01:35:09.580 --> 01:35:17.090
The fleet will be ready for a final long-distance warp in three hours

01:35:17.090 --> 01:35:23.420
I want to remind everyone that our current priority is to ensure the enemy does not follow us during war

01:35:23.680 --> 01:35:30.000
We must avoid this outcome at all costs our failure in this matter could be to total catastrophic destruction

01:35:30.650 --> 01:35:37.710
Since our radar is useless during war, we will only exit subspace once we are within direct range of our solar system

01:35:37.790 --> 01:35:42.230
These measures may seem extreme, but it will reduce the likelihood of enemy pursuit

01:35:42.230 --> 01:35:47.610
I know this voyage has been difficult. Your endurance is appreciated. By current calculations

01:35:47.610 --> 01:35:53.970
We will arrive on July 23rd, 2032. If we're lucky, we'll be able to see Halley's comet off the starboard bow

01:35:54.750 --> 01:36:00.000
Quiet down! This is our final challenge, and I implore you to remain steady

01:36:00.030 --> 01:36:01.880
fast to the end. That is all.

01:36:05.210 --> 01:36:06.140
Well,

01:36:06.680 --> 01:36:08.550
not that much longer now.

01:36:08.830 --> 01:36:12.060
Shall we? Warp will begin in 20

01:36:12.060 --> 01:36:13.200
minutes and 30 seconds.

01:36:14.180 --> 01:36:16.000
All hands please report to your stations.

01:36:16.780 --> 01:36:18.860
It's hard to believe that we've almost made it

01:36:18.860 --> 01:36:20.740
back to Earth already. Once we're planet

01:36:20.740 --> 01:36:22.440
side, maybe I can visit your hometown

01:36:22.440 --> 01:36:24.740
and then I could try to find your mother

01:36:24.740 --> 01:36:27.080
and I...

01:36:27.080 --> 01:36:29.860
then I... I can't...

01:36:34.000 --> 01:36:36.160
Warp will begin in 20 minutes.

01:36:36.160 --> 01:36:38.690
Now switching to emergency power.

01:36:38.690 --> 01:36:43.230
So, once we land, what kind of food do you want to get first?

01:36:43.230 --> 01:36:44.920
I don't care about that.

01:36:44.920 --> 01:36:49.060
I want to go shopping and see how much the styles have changed since we left.

01:36:49.060 --> 01:36:53.340
Man, would you buy some swimsuits and go to the kids?

01:36:53.340 --> 01:36:56.770
Warp will begin in 30 seconds.

01:36:56.770 --> 01:36:57.850
How is she?

01:36:57.850 --> 01:36:59.020
The gunbuster, I mean.

01:36:59.020 --> 01:37:00.000
Good.

01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:05.040
some more time to finish checking the degeneracy reactor well to be honest with you my hope is that

01:37:05.040 --> 01:37:09.760
we'll be able to make it back to earth without having to use her still keep up the good work we

01:37:09.760 --> 01:37:18.140
will sir captain we're ready to begin very well then we can start destination soul system confirmed

01:37:18.140 --> 01:37:25.830
copy engage subspace engine engaging warp will begin in 10 seconds all crew prepare to enter

01:37:25.830 --> 01:37:29.700
subspace engage warp drive engaging warp

01:38:18.720 --> 01:38:19.980
They're making enemy fire!

01:38:19.980 --> 01:38:22.060
An attack? But that's impossible!

01:38:22.060 --> 01:38:25.400
Newtonian mechanics shouldn't be able to function in subspace!

01:38:25.400 --> 01:38:30.000
We know they can't use radar either, so how did they manage to find us?

01:38:30.480 --> 01:38:32.000
Open all gun ports!

01:38:32.000 --> 01:38:33.200
What's our target?

01:38:33.200 --> 01:38:35.250
Anything! Just fire!

01:38:35.250 --> 01:38:45.050
Combat! Prepare retaliation!

01:38:45.050 --> 01:38:47.760
All hands, report to level one battle stations!

01:38:47.760 --> 01:38:51.280
Repeat! All hands, report to level one battle stations!

01:38:51.280 --> 01:38:56.400
Have they attacked any of the other ships yet?

01:38:56.400 --> 01:38:57.510
What's their status?

01:38:57.510 --> 01:39:00.000
Nothing! As long as we're still in subspace, the radar can-

01:39:00.060 --> 01:39:11.250
tell us anything we have to leave warp now please sir we're trapped there's a

01:39:11.250 --> 01:39:18.590
plasma leak in hager three now exiting subspace abort we can't warp out now

01:39:18.590 --> 01:39:25.220
we'll be leading the aliens right to us negative sir it's too late

01:39:55.280 --> 01:39:56.860
Give me a damage report on the fleet.

01:39:57.680 --> 01:40:00.000
Only 12% have been able to leave subspace.

01:40:00.600 --> 01:40:02.500
All of the smaller ships are destroyed.

01:40:02.500 --> 01:40:03.940
I see.

01:40:03.940 --> 01:40:05.760
Wait, hang on!

01:40:05.760 --> 01:40:08.640
Make that twelve signatures total other than ours!

01:40:08.640 --> 01:40:10.700
It looks like the rest of them are all the enemy!

01:40:34.320 --> 01:40:38.780
begin departure as soon as possible your top priority is to defend the ship no

01:40:38.780 --> 01:40:42.590
matter what you there what are you standing around for

01:40:42.590 --> 01:40:47.440
coach there's something wrong with the left gyro and Linda's neck simple enough

01:40:47.440 --> 01:40:50.940
Linda I want you to get in Takiya's mech and go in her place

01:40:50.940 --> 01:40:58.040
yes sir Takiya you're on standby

01:41:21.080 --> 01:41:30.000
Squadron and the remaining mechs have successfully launched engineers prioritize areas with a level damage for repairs mr. Kikuchi

01:41:30.080 --> 01:41:31.000
What's the enemy's status?

01:41:31.380 --> 01:41:33.380
Sir, we can see 22 ships so far.

01:41:33.680 --> 01:41:37.880
We believe that one of them is leading the rest and they are currently moving at around 10% life speed.

01:41:38.040 --> 01:41:40.060
The rest are surrounding us and keeping pace.

01:41:40.440 --> 01:41:41.400
Nothing else so far.

01:41:43.320 --> 01:41:46.290
Well then, it's our move, isn't it, Commander?

01:41:47.930 --> 01:41:50.750
Set crosshairs on the largest target the radar's showing.

01:41:50.930 --> 01:41:52.050
Prepare for barrage!

01:41:52.560 --> 01:41:54.200
Charge all photons or beetles!

01:41:54.360 --> 01:41:55.440
Open the launch tubes!

01:41:55.890 --> 01:41:57.910
Roger, opening the launch tubes.

01:42:00.380 --> 01:42:01.780
Calculations complete!

01:42:01.780 --> 01:42:03.880
Air compensation 3 degrees vertical.

01:42:03.880 --> 01:42:05.380
All torpedoes are ready to fire!

01:42:05.380 --> 01:42:07.520
Then commence firing now!

01:42:07.520 --> 01:42:26.920
Live after a direct hit!

01:42:26.920 --> 01:42:28.790
That shouldn't be possible!

01:42:28.790 --> 01:42:30.000
They really are monsters.

01:42:30.670 --> 01:42:33.470
Sir, we're seeing multiple smaller hostiles closing in now.

01:42:34.300 --> 01:42:36.340
Approximately 20 seconds until contact.

01:42:37.060 --> 01:42:39.760
Get those gun ports open again. Return fire!

01:42:43.520 --> 01:42:57.640
There's more!

01:43:14.590 --> 01:43:23.000
I go out there again I'll die. Even coach has given up on me. I guess I really can't help anyone

01:43:23.000 --> 01:43:30.000
and I don't blame them. Look at me. They could be dying right now and I'm just sitting

01:43:32.040 --> 01:43:33.040
a baby.

01:43:33.040 --> 01:43:36.400
Why can't I make myself stop?

01:43:36.400 --> 01:43:38.300
Is this...

01:43:38.300 --> 01:43:40.960
Is this really all I'm good for?

01:43:40.960 --> 01:43:46.490
No...

01:43:46.490 --> 01:43:48.160
Linda...

01:43:48.160 --> 01:43:49.200
Eww.

01:44:18.720 --> 01:44:30.000
what do we do person I was she died with

01:44:30.060 --> 01:44:40.690
you. Whoever I am now has to live in her place. No more crying. No more weakness. I'm going

01:44:40.690 --> 01:44:55.680
to protect them all. Destroyed. Top Squadron has suffered 42% casualties. Laser cannon's

01:44:55.680 --> 01:44:59.700
almost gone. Third bridge is destroyed. Report from heavy cruiser Bozo.

01:45:02.400 --> 01:45:04.510
Tell me, where is the enemy leader?

01:45:04.510 --> 01:45:06.340
They're above us, sir.

01:45:06.340 --> 01:45:10.650
35 degrees starboard, 12,000 kilometers.

01:45:10.650 --> 01:45:13.170
Set primary engines to critical output.

01:45:13.170 --> 01:45:17.300
We're gonna ram the bastard before they can take us out.

01:45:17.300 --> 01:45:19.580
But Captain...

01:45:19.580 --> 01:45:25.620
No matter what, we cannot allow them to reach Earth!

01:45:25.620 --> 01:45:27.230
Captain!

01:45:27.230 --> 01:45:28.150
What now?

01:45:28.150 --> 01:45:30.000
It looks like hatch 7 just opened!

01:45:30.000 --> 01:45:30.610
What?

01:46:00.320 --> 01:46:02.180
No one to ram them, not you!

01:46:02.180 --> 01:46:03.300
Takeya!

01:46:03.300 --> 01:46:05.300
Takeya, I want you to go directly for their leader.

01:46:05.300 --> 01:46:07.300
Ignore all the smaller ones.

01:46:07.300 --> 01:46:09.400
Coach.

01:46:09.400 --> 01:46:10.400
Sir!

01:46:10.400 --> 01:46:11.400
What are you doing?

01:46:11.400 --> 01:46:12.400
Go now!

01:46:12.400 --> 01:46:13.280
Alright!

01:46:34.120 --> 01:46:34.710
What is that?

01:47:08.090 --> 01:47:14.870
cruiser fermion sir so that means it's just us and the gunbuster now do we know

01:47:14.870 --> 01:47:30.000
what her status is she's engaging their leader but she's struggling it's going

01:47:30.060 --> 01:47:43.760
I've only got two minutes left.

01:47:43.760 --> 01:47:45.070
I have to catch it.

01:47:45.070 --> 01:47:46.900
I will!

01:48:01.310 --> 01:48:14.310
Smith, I'm begging you, protect me!

01:49:10.360 --> 01:49:12.400
What happened to the Gunbuster?

01:49:12.400 --> 01:49:16.290
I think... it must have disintegrated in the blast, Captain.

01:49:16.290 --> 01:49:18.640
Radar has been restored.

01:49:18.640 --> 01:49:22.560
There's no sign of the enemy. They must be retreating beyond this system.

01:49:22.560 --> 01:49:25.760
Wait! I see it! Gunbuster!

01:52:42.000 --> 01:52:46.800
Oh, jeez, this is embarrassing, but doesn't this art look fantastic?

01:52:47.040 --> 01:52:48.620
I wonder what's in store for us next.

01:52:49.220 --> 01:52:52.560
Next time on Gunbuster, we only have the titles so far.

01:52:52.880 --> 01:52:55.730
Episode 5, please, there's time enough for love.

01:52:55.990 --> 01:52:58.490
Then, final episode, at the end of eternity.

01:52:58.930 --> 01:53:00.000
Oh, I almost forgot.

01:53:23.710 --> 01:53:30.000
It's time now to present your diplomas to begin from the Okinawa branch of the Earth Imperial State.

01:53:30.000 --> 01:53:37.130
Space Force's Girls Pilot High School, cadet number two from senior class two, Miss Kazumi Amano.

01:53:37.350 --> 01:53:37.770
Here.

01:53:41.440 --> 01:53:45.960
After we got back from space, they held a special graduation for Miss Amano and me.

01:53:47.300 --> 01:53:50.770
It feels weird, like time is just passing us by.

01:53:51.540 --> 01:53:53.310
Which makes sense, I guess.

01:53:53.310 --> 01:54:00.000
I only attended this school for a few months, but in Earth time, ten years.

01:54:00.000 --> 01:54:04.260
Ten years have come and gone since I've been here.

01:54:04.260 --> 01:54:06.250
Reiko decided to stay.

01:54:06.250 --> 01:54:09.770
She's working as one of the instructors now.

01:54:09.770 --> 01:54:14.260
But the rest of my classmates have gone on without me.

01:54:14.260 --> 01:54:16.850
Even Kimiko.

01:54:16.850 --> 01:54:22.190
It's been so long, I'd be surprised if she even remembers me.

01:54:22.190 --> 01:54:26.530
And now from Senior Class 1, Miss Noriko Takaya!

01:54:26.530 --> 01:54:27.650
Here!

01:54:37.580 --> 01:54:39.840
Only 17 and officially graduated.

01:54:40.140 --> 01:54:43.140
Kind of makes me feel like one of those smart kids that get to skip a grade.

01:54:43.320 --> 01:54:45.900
True enough, though Earth won't see it quite the same.

01:54:46.300 --> 01:54:49.320
According to your birth certificate, you're graduating at 27.

01:54:49.950 --> 01:54:54.580
Well, when you put it like that, I'm actually right around the age where most people start having kids.

01:54:54.760 --> 01:54:55.800
How crazy is that?

01:55:03.550 --> 01:55:06.080
Excuse me, but are you-

01:55:06.080 --> 01:55:10.650
Noriko Takuya.

01:55:10.650 --> 01:55:11.690
Kimiko?

01:55:11.690 --> 01:55:17.780
Mm-hmm.

01:55:17.780 --> 01:55:20.230
Hitomi and Ritsuko got married?

01:55:20.230 --> 01:55:23.770
Jeez, I really am out of the loop.

01:55:23.770 --> 01:55:27.200
And on top of all of that, you're a mom now.

01:55:27.200 --> 01:55:29.800
Hey, how old is Takami?

01:55:30.000 --> 01:55:31.800
She's just about to turn three.

01:55:31.800 --> 01:55:34.320
Hmm...

01:55:34.320 --> 01:55:38.680
Huh? What's that?

01:55:38.680 --> 01:55:42.250
That's the Eltrium.

01:55:42.250 --> 01:55:44.450
Whoa! A ship?

01:55:44.450 --> 01:55:48.790
Yeah. You don't even need binoculars to see it from all the way down here.

01:55:48.790 --> 01:55:53.450
So big!

01:55:53.450 --> 01:55:56.560
They say she's over 70 kilometers long.

01:55:56.560 --> 01:56:00.000
It's how they plan to evacuate Earth, if necessary.

01:56:02.780 --> 01:56:08.780
Rumor is that the military gets priority, so only 1 in 4,000 civilians have a chance of making it on board.

01:56:08.780 --> 01:56:11.520
Seriously?

01:56:11.520 --> 01:56:14.110
I know you might hate me for asking.

01:56:14.110 --> 01:56:21.000
Still, could you use your connections to get a spot for Takumi at least?

01:56:21.000 --> 01:56:25.710
She's my world. She deserves a future.

01:56:25.710 --> 01:56:27.520
Kimiko...

